  "id": "vals_venezolano",
  "name": "Vals venezolano (Venezuelan waltz)",
  "family": "classical",
  "lineage": "The vals venezolano is the Venezuelan waltz, a 19th-century salon dance that became a national concert form, written for piano by composers such as Ramón Delgado Palacios and Heraclio Fernández and played by string groups of guitar, mandolin and cuatro. In the 20th century Antonio Lauro composed valses venezolanos for solo guitar that Alirio Díaz recorded and carried into the international guitar repertoire; its accompaniment habitually displaces the 3/4 with hemiola accents.",
